<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89333" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσευπορέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>procure</i> or <i>provide besides</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρήμαθ᾽ ὑμῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					36.57
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be forthcoming</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				24.97
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προ-</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>solve</i> a difficulty, or <i>acquire insight, in
			addition</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ προσευπόρησαν τοῖς πρὸ αὐτῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procl.
					<u>in Euc.</u>
					p.66
				</span></i>
			 F., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hyp.</u>
				7.57
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
